// How climate changes during a run. Values tuned 2026-11-14 so that over 5,000 years about 20% of
// land changes biome at some point and about 3-4% differs from the start at any one time; the
// world stays within about 1 degree C of today and regional rainfall within about 75-130%.
// May be tuned again in milestone 1 step 10.
//
// The world is divided into regions, one per cell of a coarse grid of the same kind as the map
// (frequency 4 gives 162 regions about 1,800 km across). Each region carries a temperature
// shift and a rainfall shift, and the world carries a temperature shift on top. Each shift is
// the sum of a few components that wander at random and drift back toward zero:
//   years   how long a swing typically lasts
//   spread  how large it typically is (standard deviation): degrees C for temperature, and
//           for rainfall a natural-log factor (0.15 is roughly plus or minus 15 percent)
// A cell blends the regions near it, weighted by distance, so there are no visible borders.
{
  "regionGridFrequency": 4,
  "blendRadiusKm": 1000,
  "regionTemperature": [
    { "years": 20, "spread": 0.12 },
    { "years": 300, "spread": 0.3 }
  ],
  "regionRainfall": [
    { "years": 15, "spread": 0.03 },
    { "years": 250, "spread": 0.07 }
  ],
  "worldTemperature": [
    { "years": 1500, "spread": 0.4 },
    { "years": 150, "spread": 0.1 }
  ],
  "worldTemperatureLimit": 2.0,
  "rainfallFactorMin": 0.5,
  "rainfallFactorMax": 1.5,
  "biomeIntervalYears": 10
}
